A Fragment is a way to group multiple elements in a React component without adding an extra node to the DOM.

Normally, in React, you must return a single element from a component. Sometimes, you don’t want an extra 
<div> just to wrap elements — that’s where Fragments come in.


import React from "react";

function App() {
  return (
    <React.Fragment>
      <h1>Hello</h1>
      <p>This is a fragment example</p>
    </React.Fragment>
  );
}

export default App;
// same like <></>